  "notes": "AAS in Dental Hygiene 'Course Sequence by Term' as published in the official 2026-2027 MCC pathway map (Academic Plan Code 3831, effective Fall 2026; map slug carries -25-26), retrieved 2026-10-01. Sequenced sum = 114.5 (13+19+10+11.5+16+15+15+15). Catalog Total Credits Required is 96-111.5; the sequenced sum exceeds it because the map repeats rows verbatim (DHE110-or-DHE112 in both Term 6 and Term 7; DHE201/DHE202 in Term 6 'Required for MCC and RSC' and again in Term 8 'Required for PC') and because credit ranges were seeded at the maximum printed value (documented convention). Repeats kept verbatim per catalog-duplicate convention, documented here; pipeline exclusion via the duplicate-code gate is accepted. Admission: basic science courses with 3.5 GPA, general education with 3.25 GPA, completed before entering the core DHE curriculum; grade of C or better in all courses, 75% or better in DHE coursework. DHE201/DHE202 (non-choice) repeat in Term 6 and Term 8 verbatim from the official 2026-2027 MCC pathway map (https://www.mesacc.edu/programs/map/dental-hygiene-aas-25-26): Term 6 'Required for MCC and RSC', Term 8 'Required for PC' (multi-college consortium). allow_repeated_courses set with this evidence. Coordinator fix 2026-10-06: verified against the official source; validated under build.py gates extended per coordinator decision 2026-10-05 (BACKLOG-18 wave 32), documented in build.py comments.",
